+// MIFARE Ultralight AES (MF0AES20): key material only, ahead of the auth/session state machine
+// (separate future phase). AES-128 DataProtKey lives at pages 0x30-0x33 but always reads back as
+// zero over the air; a key recovered by other means (dictionary, already known) is stashed here
+// in card byte order (memory[i] = key[15-i]) for display/save, mirroring the layout the recovery
+// flow will need once the poller exists. Unlike UL-C's 3DES key, which is kept in natural order.
+#define MF_ULTRALIGHT_AES_KEY_SIZE      (16)
+#define MF_ULTRALIGHT_AES_DATA_KEY_PAGE (0x30)
